@@ -182,3 +182,5 @@ Restoration uses a compositor-owned capability describing the activity, recovery
 The dedicated virtual KMS `--multi-output-restoration` probe types through primary removal and return, checks retained geometry/focus/draft, rejects a separate same-user restoration request, and activates the actual native button through kernel pointer input. `AGENT_OS_RESTORATION_CAPTURE` optionally captures its mapped active controls for verification. Secondary and total display-loss probes use that same button before asserting restored geometry; they compare every original saved placement while allowing the new floating Monitor. Physical display qualification remains separate. See `../vm-foundation/native-verification.json` for exact candidate, complete-suite and signed-image identities.
 
 Mapped collection Copy menus retain their interaction lease during GTK parent-window activation and root-focus handoffs. Protection ends after dismissal and focus release. The standalone `--self-test-popup-lease` regression uses the actual collection popup without an implicit input grab; the installed kernel List/Table/KeyValue journeys separately exercise the normal grabbing menus and reject concurrent row updates.
+
+Physical keyboard state is tracked per backend device. The logical seat receives one press and the final release for a shared key; removing a keyboard releases only keys that no remaining keyboard holds. The installed ordinary and fresh-profile kernel journeys cover overlapping Shift, partial release, removal of one and the last owner, and on-screen input rejection until all physical keys are up. Synthetic uinput devices qualify this guest path; physical keyboard hardware remains separate qualification.
